   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"2\\left( {x + 1} \\right) - 3 = 5\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 1: Simplify each side as much as possible.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"2x + 2 - 3 = 5\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"2x + 2 - 3 = 5\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"2x - 1 = 5\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2: Collect the variable terms on one side.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"2x - 1 = 5\"></span></p>\n<p>There is nothing to do here.</p>\n<p>Step 3: Collect the constant terms on the other side.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"2x - 1 + 1 = 5 + 1\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"2x = 6\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 4: Make the coefficient of the variable term equal to 1.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{2x}}{3} = \\frac{6}{3}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"x = 3\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 5: Checking is left to you.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"x = 3\">x = 3</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
